 "transcript": {
  "answer": "I can't give you an AUD-to-peso rate from my data. The Reserve Bank of Australia doesn't publish one for the Argentine peso (ARS), and none of my sources include it. I'd also rather not guess, because the peso moves a lot and anything from memory could be well out of date.\n\n**What I can tell you:**\n- On **16 October 2026**, A$1 bought **US$0.6947**. That's the RBA's 4pm rate, the most recent available.\n- So far in October 2026, the rate has stayed between about US$0.693 and US$0.700.\n\n**How to work out the peso rate:** multiply 0.6947 by the current number of pesos per US dollar.\n- For example, if US$1 buys 1,400 pesos, then A$1 buys about 0.6947 × 1,400 ≈ 973 pesos. The 1,400 is just an example, not a real rate.\n- You can get the current peso rate from Argentina's central bank or a live currency site.\n- Argentina has had more than one exchange rate at times, such as the official rate and the informal \"blue\" rate. If you're going to exchange cash, check which rate you'll actually get.",
